2	  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
3	  "$id": "urn:opensip:product-v1:workflows:policy-document",
4	  "title": "PolicyDocumentV1, ScopeDocumentV1, WaiverSetV1 \u2014 the closed declarative policy DSL (PROPOSED)",
5	  "description": "A policy is data. Every construct is a closed object with a fixed 'op' or field set; there is no string expression language, no script, hook, include, or reference to repository code. The predicate grammar is exactly the evaluator's predicate set from the identity contract \u00a74 (exists, none, count-at-most, all-covered, and, or, not) over typed fact-field filters, evaluated with strong Kleene three-valued logic. Bounds: at most 512 rules; at most 64 predicate nodes per rule; nesting depth at most 8; at most 16 filters per atom; at most 4096 waivers. Policy, scope and resolved waiver digests are raw SHA-256 of the canonical closed document bytes, retained as blobs; they are not H-domain identities.",
