16	      "type": "string",
17	      "description": "A resolution rung NAME. This replaces the withdrawn abstract Resolution tier vocabulary (syntax/resolved/type/external), which was disjoint from the rung names every fact, Coverage entry and native RequirementV2 actually carries, had no published mapping onto them, and was compared by a single global rank table across all relations. The inherited C-1 law is that ordering is PER-RELATION and never global, so an abstract tier could only ever be a partial, lossy, relation-dependent renaming of the rung it names; the atom now names the rung directly. This enum is the flat vocabulary and is a NECESSARY condition only: it is exactly the union of the ladders in foundation/relation-payload-schemas.v2.json#/x-opensip-relation-registry (the single ladder authority) and is drift-checked against it. Membership of THIS atom's relation's ladder is the sufficient condition and is enforced at admission, because no schema keyword can express it without restating the ladders and creating another independent source.",
